      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))&=(- (t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) - (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+((t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + (t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,\\mathbf{j}\\\\&=(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})=- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
